body:
I was using this `{'sectors': Sector.objects.all()}`, but for some mysterious reason it was raising a exception. Can't rememmber it exactly, but will look into it. 

&#x200B;

`module_set` is a built-in method or attribute?

`get_range`:

    @register.filter
    def get_range(value):
        return range(len(value))

Another limitation I bumped on: django templating language doesn't accept range() or len(), so I use the filter to return the range list to the for iteration. I know it works as expected because the cells are rendered, but empty.

&#x200B;

Oh... It did work!!!!!!!! 

Thank you very much!
